{
 "_comment": "Round 64, features 3 and 5: what every SDK signs, sends and reads for an account stop and a member key's tool allowlist (orchestrator internal/artifacts/account_stop.go StopSubject, internal/api/account_stop.go, internal/api/accounts.go readAllowedTools, internal/auth/allowlist.go). The owner's request key signs a stop (account.stopped) or a resume (account.resumed) over the owner-change preimage (verdifax.owner-change-signature.v1, the account, the change, the subject, signed_at and nonce, joined by zero bytes) with the subject: the action, key=<the owner key's id>, for a stop signoffs=<accept or refuse> and webhooks=<continue or pause> (defaults accept and continue), for a resume lifts=<the feed place of the stop it lifts>, and reason_sha256=<the lowercase hex SHA-256 of the reason's UTF-8 bytes, or nothing>, joined by single spaces. A reason is at most 1000 bytes; only its hash is sealed. subject_refuse lists inputs every SDK refuses before signing. A member key's allowlist is one or more distinct names from tools or the stop permission, never a name in never_granted; the server seals it sorted. GET /stats reports a key's allowlist in the X-Verdifax-Allowed-Tools header, comma-separated; no header means no allowlist. feed_kinds are the round 64 feed kinds every SDK lists and a webhook may name; an SDK reading a feed passes any kind it does not know through unchanged. The setting verdifax-stop signs the change setting.verdifax_stop. Every SDK reads this file in a test.",
